    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00002",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00187:title:sect-00002-title",
        "text": "Ultraviolet Spectroscopy"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00004",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00004"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00002",
          "class": "scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00187:caption:fig-00002-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00187:alt:fig-00002-alt",
              "text": "The ultraviolet spectrum of benzene shows peaks at 184 and 202 nanometers. Seven small peaks are between 225 to 268 nanometers"
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_15_07_002.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00003",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00187:title:sect-00003-title",
        "text": "Nuclear Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00005",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00005"
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00006",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00006"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00003",
          "class": "scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00187:caption:fig-00003-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00187:alt:fig-00003-alt",
              "text": "In an applied magnetic field, aromatic ring is oriented at 90 degrees. Labels read, circulating pi electrons, proton deshielded by induced field, and induced magnetic field because of the ring current."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_15_07_003.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00007",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00007"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00004",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00187:alt:fig-00004-alt",
              "text": "The structure and ball-and-stick model along with the electrostatic potential map of [18]annulene. In annulene, inside H, and outside H are labeled minus 3.0 delta and plus 9.3 delta, respectively."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_15_07_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00008",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00008"
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00009",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00009"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00005",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00187:alt:fig-00005-alt",
              "text": "Aromatic ring with carbon atom at C 1. The carbon is bonded to two hydrogen atoms and R group, labeled benzylic protons. Hydrogens bonded to the ring are aryl protons."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_15_07_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00010",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00010"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00006",
          "class": "scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00187:caption:fig-00006-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00187:alt:fig-00006-alt",
              "text": "The 1 H N M R spectrum of para-bromotoluene shows peaks at 0 (T M S), 2.3, 7.0, and 7.4 parts per million."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_15_07_006.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00011",
          "segmentId": "m00187:para:para-00011"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00007",
          "class": "scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00187:caption:fig-00007-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00187:alt:fig-00007-alt",
              "text": "The structures of benzene, toluene, chlorobenzene, and naphthalene with 13 C N M R spectrum values indicated."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_15_07_007.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
